kruskall for heart rate (bpm)
Heart rate (bpm) was analyzed across 43 days, from August 20 to September 30. A Kruskal-Wallis test was used to compare heart distributions between days, assessing whether any day showed a statistically different pattern. The test identified Sept 24 as significantly different from the others. In the box plot, Sept 24 is highlighted in red, while all other days are shown in blue, indicating a distinct physiological deviation on that date. Also, incidentally the resting heart rate was higher than that of all other days.
<!--begin.rcode
# Group by calendarDate and compute summary stats
stats <- tab %>%
  group_by(calendarDate) %>%
  summarise(
    Min = min(observed, na.rm = TRUE),
    Q1 = quantile(observed, 0.25, na.rm = TRUE),
    Median = median(observed, na.rm = TRUE),
    Q3 = quantile(observed, 0.75, na.rm = TRUE),
    Max = max(observed, na.rm = TRUE),
    IQR = IQR(observed, na.rm = TRUE),
    .groups = "drop"
  )

# Kruskal-Wallis test across calendarDate
kruskal <- kruskal.test(observed ~ calendarDate, data = tab)

# Identify anomalous day with highest median
anomaly_day <- stats %>%
  filter(Median == max(Median)) %>%
  pull(calendarDate)

# Add color flag to tab
tab <- tab %>%
  mutate(colorFlag = ifelse(calendarDate == anomaly_day, "Anomaly", "Normal"))


# Box plot with anomaly highlight
plot_ly(
  data = tab,
  x = ~calendarDate,
  y = ~observed,
  type = "box",
  color = ~colorFlag,
  colors = c("Normal" = "#3498DB", "Anomaly" = "#E74C3C"),
  boxpoints = "all",
  jitter = 0.3,
  pointpos = 0
) %>%
  layout(
    title = "Heart Rate Box Plot by Day with Anomaly Highlighted (Kruskal-Wallis)",
    xaxis = list(title = "Date"),
    yaxis = list(title = "Heart Rate (bpm)")
  )

print(stats)
cat("\nKruskal-Wallis p-value:", kruskal$p.value, "\n")
cat("Anomalous day identified:", anomaly_day, "\n")

end.rcode-->


